## Controlled comparisons (ckpt-1000; first arm relative to second)

- **CYLORI27 vs P1ORI27** (KEY: CylDINO + cue vs FLAC + cue — isolates CERPA with the conditioning information fixed): K=8 T60 +6.4% · C50 +15.5% · EDT +12.6% · R@1 +6.2% · R@10 +2.3%; K=1 T60 +5.5% · C50 +15.8% · EDT +13.6% · R@1 +0.5% · R@10 +2.0%
- **P1ORI27 vs P1** (does the cue alone help vanilla FLAC?): K=8 T60 -2.7% · C50 -15.1% · EDT -10.3% · R@1 -9.8% · R@10 -3.0%; K=1 T60 -3.5% · C50 -14.6% · EDT -9.0% · R@1 -8.3% · R@10 -1.3%
- **YAWORI27 vs YAW** (does the cue restore what yaw augmentation removed?): K=8 T60 -19.3% · C50 -30.5% · EDT -20.4% · R@1 +18.8% · R@10 +12.5%; K=1 T60 -17.7% · C50 -30.4% · EDT -18.2% · R@1 +14.4% · R@10 +11.8%
- **CYLORI27 vs P1** (CylDINO + cue vs plain FLAC (exp_23 headline)): K=8 T60 +3.5% · C50 -2.0% · EDT +1.0% · R@1 -4.3% · R@10 -0.8%; K=1 T60 +1.8% · C50 -1.0% · EDT +3.5% · R@1 -7.8% · R@10 +0.7%
- **CYLORI27 vs CYL** (the cue's effect on CylDINO): K=8 T60 -34.7% · C50 -37.3% · EDT -28.2% · R@1 +21.0% · R@10 +13.7%; K=1 T60 -33.2% · C50 -35.5% · EDT -25.4% · R@1 +21.0% · R@10 +14.6%
- **P1ZUP27 vs P1** (CONTROL: does a constant NON-orientation field (same scale) give vanilla FLAC the same gains as the facing cue?): K=8 T60 -2.3% · C50 -15.3% · EDT -11.1% · R@1 -10.1% · R@10 -2.8%; K=1 T60 -3.2% · C50 -14.6% · EDT -9.6% · R@1 -5.8% · R@10 -1.6%
- **P1ORI27 vs P1ZUP27** (facing cue vs constant-up field on vanilla FLAC (information beyond the bias effect?)): K=8 T60 -0.4% · C50 +0.2% · EDT +0.8% · R@1 +0.3% · R@10 -0.2%; K=1 T60 -0.3% · C50 +0.1% · EDT +0.7% · R@1 -2.6% · R@10 +0.3%

